---
description: Shared UI and web styling conventions
globs: apps/web/**,packages/ui/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# UI

- Whimsical light-first (+ soft dark); **Lexend** (display + body/tiles default) + optional **Jersey 15** display; Sage Garden tokens from `packages/ui` theme (cream / sage / potato gold — **never** purple/indigo clones).
- **Fonts via CSS vars only — never per-component face swaps.** `theme.css`: `--font-pixel` / `--font-clean` → `--font-display` / `--font-body` / `--font-sans`. Tailwind `fontFamily.sans|body|display` (preset **theme root**, not extend) map to those vars so preflight doesn’t paint `ui-sans-serif`. `html, body, #root` also set `var(--font-sans)`. Cold path ships Lexend **latin 400/500/600/700** (`index.css`); Jersey 15 latin loads on demand when Pixel Titles is on. **Pixel type** pref (`fontPreference`, default `clean`) sets `html[data-font="pixel"|"clean"]`, which retargets `--font-display` only (`pixel` → Jersey 15). Body/tiles stay `--font-clean`. **`--font-display-tracking`**: clean `-0.01em`, pixel `0.06em` (Jersey 15 reads cramped without open tracking) — headings / `.font-display` / word pill consume it; Lexend body untouched. Toggle on **Options** `/options`; `applyFontPreference` on boot. **Do not** hardcode Jersey 15/Lexend/system stacks in JSX or one-off CSS — change the vars. RN-web `Text` (`.css-text-*`): inherit `font-family` / `font-weight` / `letter-spacing` from parent chrome so `.cp-hud-bubble` / `.cp-run-badge` bold actually applies; `font-display`/`font-body` + `font-medium|semibold|bold` on the Text re-assert with `!important`. Play Spin chips use **`font-body`** (not display) so Pixel Titles doesn’t Jersey the board controls. `Button`: `cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size }), className)` so `className` can twMerge-override variant fonts.
- **Token roles** (`packages/ui/src/theme.css` + `tailwind-preset`):
  - **primary** = sage — main actions, path, board chrome
  - **secondary** = potato gold — warm brand accent (score badge, selected mode cards, secondary buttons, hard challenge)
  - **accent** = soft sage — hover/soft wash only (not a second brand)
  - **muted** = soft sage-gray — chip/segment tracks, ghost hover
  - **icon-muted-foreground** = decorative lobby section/pref glyphs (dark: lifted vs helper `muted-foreground`)
  - Prefer `bg-secondary` / `text-secondary` / `text-secondary-foreground`; `--potato` is an alias of secondary (legacy)
  - **Medal / potato glyphs without a solid secondary fill:** use `text-secondary` (visible gold in dark). Never bare `text-secondary-foreground` on charcoal/`muted` — dark `--secondary-foreground` is near-black and goes invisible. Pair `text-secondary-foreground` only with `bg-secondary` (or a strong secondary wash).
  - **Palette locked to the logo mascot** (`packages/ui/src/assets/logo.png`, potato-on-armchair): sampled chair sage `#9aad86` (lit) / `#717d66` (shadow) / `#c1d1ab` (highlight) → olive/warm, not minty; sampled potato gold `#d3b062` / `#ad804b` → muted tan, not peachy-orange. `--primary #859075`, `--secondary #d8b05b`, `--accent #b5c5a0`, board `#444a3c`/`#6a735d`/`#a1af8e`. Re-sample from the logo before nudging further; don't drift back cooler/pinker.
- **UI inspiration (steal craft, keep brand):**
  - [TypeUI](https://www.typeui.sh/) thinking: design-system tokens first, then hierarchy / spacing rhythm / type leading / interaction feedback as the reasoning layer. Steep display→label contrast; motion for entrance, feedback, transition only; depth via luminance + surface — not flat robot UI.
  - Tactile word-game refs (user CleanShot set): pillow cream tiles, thick rounded board frame, circular select (square) / hex tile tint + drop-shadow ring (Honeycomb) + juicy path stroke, word pill (live swipe: no pts badge), atmospheric background. No Scrabble TW/TL multipliers. **Selected tiles** use centralized `--tile-select-*` tokens (deeper sage wash + ring vs cream idle tiles — must read at a glance). Hex select is the clipped tile itself (`HEX_CLIP`) so `--cp-tile-gap` gutters cannot offset a separate overlay; path SVG shares `.cp-board-play` with the tile grid.
- **Motion:** any meaningful interactivity should show the change — short CSS/NativeWind transitions/feedback (segment pill slide, select pop, Goal↔Timed swap, button press, path/score ticks, screen enter). Keep whimsical, light, performant. Prefer CSS; don’t animate everything mindlessly; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. No anime.js unless CSS can’t cover it.
- **Accordions / collapsibles:** always animate open/close (height via CSS grid `0fr`→`1fr`, opacity, chevron rotate). Prefer that pattern (or shadcn `Collapsible` if already in tree) over raw `<details>` with an instant snap. Instant open/close only under `prefers-reduced-motion`. Lobby **Min length** is always-visible choice cards (same `.cp-lobby-challenge` pattern as How hard?), not an accordion.
- **UI package ownership (hard rule):** `@couch-potato/ui` (`packages/ui`) owns shared presentational UI (board, marks/sprites, Shell, empty/loading, score/confetti/progress, BrandHeader / ScrollShell / PrefChoiceGroup / TimerRing / WordGroups, and any chrome widget Expo should share). **`apps/web/src/components` is not a design system.** Allowed there: (1) `components/ui/*` = thin shadcn/Radix wrappers only, (2) route/feature composition that imports from `@couch-potato/ui` + shadcn + app storage/router (`ChromeNav`, `HomeSetup`, `CommandPalette`, `PlaySkeleton`, medals/board wiring, …). Before adding a new file under `apps/web/src/components/` (outside `ui/`), ask: is this reusable presentational? → put it in `packages/ui`. See `AGENTS.md` Stack.
- **Web chrome:** shadcn/ui (Radix + Tailwind) is the preferred base for Button/input/dialog/toast/command — customize (toy press shadows), don’t hand-roll duplicates. **Command palette:** ⌘K / Ctrl+K → `CommandPalette` (`cmdk` `CommandDialog`) for chrome jumps (Lobby, Play, How to play, Options, Couch crew, Couch medals, Last results) **and** inline Options pref flips (one verb action each — Switch Look to Day/Night, Use Clean/Pixel titles, Hide/Show words left, Turn SFX/Lobby jam on/off — same setters as `/options`, close after apply; keywords: dark, sound, pixel, words left, music, jam, bgm, etc.). Selected row = `bg-primary` + `text-primary-foreground` (cream on sage — never dark ink on primary fill). Quiet md+ affordance: shadcn `Kbd` chip in `ChromeNav` (after icons, platform ⌘/Ctrl; click → `openCommandPalette`); hidden below md. Game board (`LetterGrid`, path, tile drop, confetti) stays custom + tactile. Board cast shadow lives on non-rotating `.cp-board-frame`; only `.cp-board-spin` rotates (see `AGENTS.md` Rotate).
- **Chrome consistency:** **no soft window-pane cards** (big gooey radius, frosted/translucent fills, inset glass highlights, multi-layer glow rings). Surfaces are **pixel-block**: `--radius: 0.25rem`, opaque `var(--card)` / `var(--muted)`, **2px** solid borders, active = potato/sage border + fill wash (no blur halo). HUD status pills may stay `rounded-full` (pill chrome ≠ window pane). **Chunky toy** (inset highlight + offset shadow) reserved for **Play CTA** (`Button` default/secondary) and **board frame/tiles** only — board uses its own slightly softer tile/frame radii (`0.35rem` / `0.75rem`), independent of chrome `--radius`. Icon toggles: potato ring + fill + glyph motion when on. New surfaces follow pixel-block — don’t invent a third glass tier.
- **Lobby Play CTA:** sticky-bar star gets `.cp-play-cta` — chunky inset+offset shadow, hover lift/scale (~1.03) + **fresher sage** (`primary`↔`accent` lift — never muddy potato-olive or `brightness()` dunk), press sink with deeper sage lip inset, loud potato `focus-visible` ring; `prefers-reduced-motion` = color/border only. Default `Button` primary shares the same accent-lift hover + deeper-sage press. **Secondary** (`Button` secondary / Play Spin chips): light mode = soft potato↔card wash (solid `#d8b05b` slabs read too heavy on cream); dark = solid secondary. No `brightness()` hover.
- **Copy / voice:** prefer **gaming terminology** (Play, lobby, run, haul, SFX, spin, Couch crew) over sterile app/form words (Submit, Settings, Confirm). Whimsical Couch Potato: clear for casual players, not esports jargon. **Never use em dashes (—)** in player-facing copy (UI strings, toasts, tooltips/`aria-label`, SEO titles/descriptions); prefer comma, period, or a hyphen sparingly. Icon tooltips/`aria-label` match that voice.
- **Prefer icons** for controls/options when the glyph is faster (sound, pause, rotate, couch crew, Options; lobby chips): `lucide-react` + `aria-label` + shadcn `IconTooltip` (hover/focus; Radix long-press on touch — don’t rely on tooltip alone). Drop native `title` when Tooltip is present (double chrome). `TooltipContent` / `IconTooltip` use `font-display` (pixel type follows the pref). Keep lobby mode/challenge labeled; mid-run **End run** lives in the Escape/pause menu (same bottom row as **Resume**, End run left | Resume right, after prefs) and ends the run immediately — except **early quit** (within 3s of board ready): End run / Leave run → lobby, no results. Lobby glyphs get lucide + `.cp-lobby-glyph` hover/press juice. **Section titles** get a muted decorative lucide icon beside the label (same size/weight as Show words left eye) — lobby sections, Results haul/missed (`Sparkles` / `Sofa`), Couch medals (`Medal`, potato `text-secondary`), Potato Board (`Trophy` / `Star` / `History`); mode cards keep their own glyphs. **Play spin** (board turn under the grid): compact chips — `RotateCcwSquare`/`RotateCwSquare` + short “Spin” label, tip/aria “Spin board left/right” — plain `RotateCcw`/`RotateCw` alone reads as undo/redo; never `Undo2`/history metaphors. Same row height as before (no board shrink).
- **Active / selected / on states must be obvious** (color + ring + weight), not a subtle border-only change. Selected lobby glyphs use potato `text-secondary` (or `text-secondary-foreground` on a secondary wash like Hard / Words left on); inactive stay `text-muted-foreground`. Soft lucide fill (`fillOpacity` ~0.22) amps selected. Don’t use `text-primary` alone for “on” on cream: sage primary ≈ muted-foreground and reads as still-off.
- **Icon-only motion:** Button `size="icon"` / `icon-sm` → shared `.cp-icon-btn` (hover lift + scale ~1.12 + sage `accent`/`primary` wash when off, active squash, `aria-pressed` potato ring + pulse). **Pref toggles** (music/SFX): `variant="outline"` off (muted border/fill), hover = sage accent (not muddy potato-on-cream), `aria-pressed="true"` potato wash + ring — not filled `secondary` CTAs. CSS only; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. `aria-pressed` = feature **on**, not muted. Icon tooltips: feature + state (`SFX on` / `Music off`). **Music icons:** `Music2` on, local `MusicOff` off (not Volume; those are SFX).
- **Active icon toggles need on-state motion, not just color/ring.** Ring/pulse alone (`.cp-icon-btn[aria-pressed="true"]`) reads static — the glyph itself must move while the feature is on. Give the "on" icon a shared `apps/web/src/index.css` utility class (`.cp-icon-anim-note` note bob for `Music2`/BGM, `.cp-icon-anim-wave` speaker pulse for `Volume2`/SFX; add siblings for new toggles, don't scope to `.cp-icon-btn` so any active glyph can opt in) instead of a one-off animation. Only the "on" icon renders the class — the "off" icon (`MusicOff`/`VolumeX`) stays static, no ternary needed. Keyframes/animation live only inside `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`; `reduce` sets `animation: none` (ring/color still shows the on state). CSS only, no anime.js.
- **Chrome nav icons** (Back to lobby when not on `/` / Couch medals / Couch crew / Options): lobby `Sofa` is leftmost and **hidden on lobby** (no self-link); other routes use `aria-current="page"` for potato wash + ring + soft lucide fill; hover inactive = sofa bounce / medal bob / crew nudge / gear tilt (`.cp-icon-anim-sofa|medal|crew|gear`); active page keeps a gentler idle; `prefers-reduced-motion` = color/fill only. md+ only: muted `Kbd` ⌘K/Ctrl+K after icons (not a CTA; opens palette).
- **Options / Couch break prefs:** 2-option **choice cards** (`.cp-lobby-challenge`, same as How hard? / Min length) — not iOS switches. `/options`: hero `LogoOptions` (gear-in-hand mascot) + Look / Titles / Words left / Sound effects / Lobby jam on `ScrollShell` + `cp-shell-options` / `cp-options` (widens on md+); `.cp-options-prefs` stacks on phone, 2-col ≥36rem container, 3-col ≥44rem so a desktop viewport fits without scrolling. **Replay how-to** = secondary chrome CTA (not a choice-card pair) → clears `howToSeen`, opens `/how-to`. Hints only where the choice isn’t obvious (e.g. Words left Hide/Show) — skip Day/Night, Sound effects, Lobby jam. Couch break IA: Sound effects / Lobby jam / Words left / Look, then bottom run controls separated by a pixel-block `border-t-2 border-border` + `pt-3`. Phone: **End run | Restart** on one row, full-width **Resume** under (3-up crushes labels). sm+: one row **End run | Restart | Resume** (End ghost/`cp-end-run-btn` | Restart outline | Resume primary). Restart discards the open run (no results) and gens a fresh board with the same lobby launch. Never park Resume above the prefs. Selected = potato `secondary` glyph + sage active border (must read clearly as on vs off). Device prefs live on **`/options`** only (not lobby setup, Couch crew, Customize your game, or Play bar) — Sound effects + Lobby jam also in Couch break mid-run. Dark mode also in Couch break mid-run.
- **Web cursors:** lean global rule in `apps/web/src/index.css` (`button`, `[role=button]`, `a[href]`, `summary`, labels/inputs) — don’t sprinkle `cursor-pointer` per class. Letter board: `grab` / `grabbing` while swiping. Tile hit acceptance uses `--cp-tile-gap` gutters + `isInTileHitZone` edge inset (dead zone between letters). Path backtrack (revisit → pop/truncate) only in the tile **center zone** (`isInBacktrackZone` / `allowBacktrack`) so diagonal transit that clips a previous corner does not false-pop.
- `packages/ui` RN Button = Expo/RN path; web app chrome → shadcn. Don’t maintain two competing web Buttons.
- Mobile-first; minimize one-off Tailwind in routes.
- **Home lobby IA:** toy cards/tiles (`HomeSetup`) — not stacked MODE/GRID label+segment rows. **Primary** (what am I playing): mode → board → challenge. **Customize your game** (advanced column, quieter): min length + **Ban list** pillbox (`WordBanInput` — Enter to tag a playable word, Backspace/× to remove; device `customBlockedWords`). Lobby hydrates from **last-played** launch (`loadLaunch` — session + durable last-launch). Phone *and* tablet: single stack primary → advanced. Wide web (`.cp-lobby-columns` container ≥44rem — only the lg Shell tier, ~1024px viewport; deliberately wider than the ≥36rem brand-row breakpoint so the advanced column has real room instead of a 36rem-tight squeeze): primary left | advanced right; cards hug content (`align-items: start`, no stretch). Sticky Play outside scroller = Play (+ compact **Last results** / Last haul `History` when this profile has a persisted last run — opens full `/results`; no music/SFX / theme / font toggles). On md+ lobby, that cluster max ~28rem centered (phone stays full-width dominant Play). Header chrome: **Back to lobby** (`Sofa`, leftmost, hidden on `/`) / **Couch medals** / **Couch crew** / **Options** icon buttons → `/`, `/achievements`, `/profiles`, `/options`. Renders on lobby + Achievements + Couch crew + Options (`ChromeNav`). **Couch crew** = profiles + Potato Board + medals — not theme/font. Device prefs = **Options** page only.
- **Brand lockup:** every chrome page shows product name **Couch Potato** + a mascot mark via `BrandHeader` (`@couch-potato/ui`). Optional `title` (Options / Couch medals / outcome) and `description` (tagline, medal count) — descriptions are not required. Lobby uses `brandHeading` so the wordmark is the page `<h1>`. **Play** stays HUD-only (no brand header mid-run). 404 / 500 / Results reuse the same lockup with page-specific marks.
- **Home lobby width (web):** Shell default stays `max-w-md` (**play** stays narrow). Lobby Home adds `cp-shell-lobby` (wider at md/lg/xl in `apps/web` `index.css`) + `@container lobby` on `.cp-lobby`: `BrandHeader` (`PotatoSnoreSvg` = bored atlas cell + continuous breath/Zzz — see potato-sprites) + Couch Potato + tagline; wide = logo | stacked copy). Choice rows use `.cp-lobby-choice-row-*` (`minmax(0,1fr)`); below **26rem** container (phone / max-w-md shell): 2-/3-up single-stack, duration 4-up → 2×2 — when cards single-stack, keep **text + glyphs centered** like the rest of the phone lobby (don’t leave a left-aligned island). Cross-platform flex + max-width; no `@container` in RN.
- **Desktop real estate (chrome pages):** any "chrome" page (lobby, Couch crew, **Results**, Achievements / Couch medals, **Options**, and similar) should widen and go multi-col on md+, never sit as a narrow `max-w-md` stick with huge empty margins at desktop widths. Pattern: `Shell` gets a dedicated wide class (`cp-shell-lobby`, `cp-shell-crew`, `cp-shell-results`, `cp-shell-medals`, `cp-shell-options`, …) sharing the same `.cp-shell.cp-shell-*` max-width scale (42rem md / 56rem lg / 64rem xl, `apps/web/src/index.css`) + its own named `@container` (`.cp-lobby`, `.cp-crew`, `.cp-results`, `.cp-medals`, `.cp-options`, …) so that page's multi-col breakpoint (~36–44rem container) is independent of others. Split content where two blocks read naturally side by side (e.g. Couch crew: crew roster | medals teaser; Results: medals full-width, then haul/missed | board replay; Achievements: The big picture | Personal bests / Length hauls | Survival via `.cp-medals-columns`; Options: pref groups via `.cp-options-prefs`) — columns are `align-items: start` / content-height, never `stretch`-to-sibling-emptiness. Phone **and** tablet stay single-stack (flex-col fallback below the container breakpoint) except Options which 2-cols once the shell clears ~36rem. **Scrollbar = viewport edge, not mid-column:** scroll a full-width wrapper (`ScrollShell` / lobby’s outer `cp-shell-scroll`), with the max-width `Shell` centered *inside* it. Never put `overflow-y-auto` on the Shell itself for chrome pages. Never use `overflow-x: hidden` on that Shell/`cp-*` container — it forces `overflow-y: auto` and traps scroll mid-column; use `overflow-x: clip` instead. **Play** stays narrow — never add a wide `cp-shell-*` there.
- **CTA width (no full-bleed desktop buttons):** chrome-page actions (`Play again`, `Back to lobby`, empty-state / 404 primaries, etc.) must **not** stretch edge-to-edge of a wide shell — this was called out repeatedly; don’t regress. Prefer content-sized / tight max-width, centered (`.cp-chrome-cta`, Results `.cp-results-actions`). Filling the column is fine only while the page itself is still play-narrow (`max-w-md`). Never bare `w-full` on a CTA under a `cp-shell-*` wide layout. Dialog / Couch break may still use full dialog width (modal column, not the desktop shell); Couch break run CTAs: phone stacks Resume under End|Restart; sm+ stays one horizontal row. **Fixed chrome max-widths** (dialogs, command palette, similar caps): use **px**, not rem — rem tracks root font size and drifts layout.
- **Play HUD IA:** one top row — primary status (`N pts left` for Goal countdown, or timer for timed/survival) + **challenge badge** (Easy/Medium/Hard for every mode — Timed duration lives on the ring, not the badge) via `.cp-run-badge` + compact icon cluster (pause only); words-left count as muted “N left” readout when on (toggle lives in Couch break + **Options** `/options` — not HUD); SFX + Lobby jam same homes (Options + Couch break — not HUD / lobby Play bar); no stacked haul/score pills (live word pill shows letters only; per-word pts on Last catch); idle pill hint = mode tagline · min length only (`Clear the couch · 3+`) — **never** repeat Easy/Medium/Hard or Timed duration (badge owns difficulty; ring owns the clock); progress under the row for Goal (bar = cleared fraction, pill = remaining); spin stays by the board. Primary pill **heats** with progress: Goal = muted → sage/`path` → potato `secondary` (`1 − remaining/target`); brief pulse on clear/haul. **Timed/Survival** = circular `TimerRing` (full at sprint length / survival budget, arc drains with remaining ms; sage/`path` → **destructive** terracotta at warn ≤ min(20s, 30% baseline), critical ≤ min(10s, 15% baseline); brief pulse on tier step; `prefers-reduced-motion` → color/dash only). **Survival** adds potato `+Ns` on the ring (`.cp-survival-bump` absolute via `.cp-survival-bump-anchor` — no HUD layout shift). Fixed 44px ring so digits never shove the challenge badge. **Leave guard:** open run → `useBlocker` confirms before chrome jumps (⌘K etc.) / history back; Leave dumps haul (no results); within 3s of board ready → lobby (no haul); Keep playing stays; `/results` finish path + beforeunload for tab close.
- **Results screen:** `ScrollShell` + `cp-shell-results` / `cp-results` (widens on md+). Staggered `cp-fade-up` + `cp-stagger-N` entrance (hero → board → columns → CTAs); hero is `BrandHeader` with dedicated marks (~96): `LogoCelebrate` on win/high score/**timeout**/any scored haul, chill `Logo` only on empty quit — not atlas `PotatoSprite` frames — + Couch Potato wordmark + reason title + run-meta badge (`.cp-run-badge` / `formatRunMeta`: Goal·Medium·3+) + unboxed `.cp-results-haul-tag` score (`cp-pop-in` beat on every outcome, even a 0 haul); new best heats potato gold on the number (`.cp-results-haul-tag-gold` + optional `.cp-results-score-sparkle`) with a quiet `.cp-results-best-label` under the score ("New couch best"), never a floating sticker on the sprite; `ConfettiBurst` for won/high-score/**timeout** (quit without a haul stays pop-in only). **Play end curtain:** every finish (`won` / `timeout` / `quit`) holds ~1.3s on Play with tile drop + confetti + outcome pill (`Couch clear!` / `Time's up!` / `Clock ran dry!` / `Haul locked!`) via `runEndFlourish.ts` before navigating to Results — not win-only. **Board replay:** medals full-width on top when present; then `.cp-results-replay` = haul+missed **left** | mini `LetterGrid` **right** alone (sticky). Phone stacks board first. Tap haul / Long ones left chips (`WordGroups` `onWordSelect`) → `findPathForWord` path highlight (`cp-word-chip-selected`). Legacy runs without letters show “Board went walkabout”. Wide:  CTAs `.cp-results-actions` = one centered hugging row (Play again primary + `CirclePlay` | Back to lobby outline + `Sofa`) — never stacked, never full-shell width; `flex-wrap` only if phone is too tight. Found/missed words render as `WordGroups` chips (`variant="found"` sage-tinted + `cp-catch-in` punch, `variant="missed"` muted, no comma walls); missed section title **Long ones left** (engine `missedLongWords` tease, not full `allWords − found` — that is Words left HUD only) + helper that short crumbs aren’t listed; collapses (`.cp-results-collapse-panel`, same 0fr/1fr recipe as `.cp-lobby-more-panel`) open by default under ~8 words, closed above. Same **Back to lobby** rule on Options / Couch crew / Achievements: `variant="outline"` + `Sofa` + `.cp-chrome-cta`, never `ghost` (sole empty-state / 404 primary CTAs stay default).
- **404 / 500 pages:** top-aligned in `ScrollShell` (never `min-h-full` + `justify-center` — that dumps a huge empty band above short chrome). `BrandHeader` + interactive `PotatoSprite` (404 crumbs: idle↔cheer crops) / static `PotatoSprite frame="idle"` (500); page title 404/500; EmptyState copy without a second mascot. CTA keeps the `Sofa` icon (`Back to lobby` convention).
- **Chrome top spacing:** chrome pages start content under Shell safe-area padding — no vertical centering of short pages. Keep brand marks in the ~64–96 range (Results hero max ~96); avoid oversized hero sprites that read as empty cream above the title.
- **Loading / empty / skeletons (quirky, layout-aware):**
  - **Voice:** loading + empty copy stays Couch Potato — whimsical game terms, not “Loading…” / “No data” / “Error occurred”. Shared helpers: `EmptyState` + `LoadingPotato` in `packages/ui` (+ thin web pages). No em dashes.
  - **Empty:** use `EmptyState` for true voids (no profiles, zero haul, no last run). Keep it short (title + optional body). `showLogo` = bored `PotatoSprite` only when the page has **no** brand mark already; never double-mascot under `BrandHeader`. Top-align in the page flow — don’t vertically center short empties in `min-h-full`.
  - **Loading — prefer skeletons.** We almost always know the chrome that will land (Options prefs grid, Couch crew roster, medals tracks, Results columns). Show a **layout skeleton** that mirrors the real structure (same shell width, card/row shapes, choice-card footprints) with muted pulse/`animate-pulse` blocks — pixel-block radii + borders, Sage tokens (`bg-muted` / soft primary wash), respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (static muted blocks, no pulse). Prefer shadcn `Skeleton` once added under `components/ui`; don’t invent a second primitive. Skeleton placeholders are silent (no “Growing potatoes…” under every row).
  - **LoadingPotato** = fallback for waits with **no stable layout to mirror** yet (bare chrome route `Suspense` before that page’s skeleton exists). Quirky message OK there. **Play** is an exception that *does* have a known IA — use `PlaySkeleton` (HUD + board tiles matching launch size **and** topology: square grid or honeycomb clip) for `/play` Suspense + pre-board-gen, never a centered potato as the Play wait. Don’t use a centered full-viewport potato as the default for chrome pages that already have a known IA.
  - **Route Suspense:** lazy chrome routes should skeleton the page chrome when practical; `LoadingPotato` in `routeTree` is acceptable until a route-specific skeleton exists — replace when that screen’s layout is settled.
- **EmptyState mascot:** `showLogo` renders pinned `PotatoSprite frame="bored"` (`/logo-snore.webp` crop) — never the chill brand `Logo`. Pages that already show a brand mark in `BrandHeader` must not duplicate under the empty copy.
- **Board size never shrinks for other play chrome** (`.cp-board-frame` = `flex-shrink: 0` in `apps/web/src/index.css`) — the board's height comes from its own aspect-ratio content, not a flex-basis, so a default-shrink flex column will squash + clip it (bottom tile row cut off against `overflow: hidden`) the moment a sibling grows. **Last catch** pill lives in one horizontal row with the rotate controls below the board (`LAST CATCH` centered between spin-left/spin-right in a `justify-center gap-2` hug cluster — not a full-width `flex-1` stretch that parks spins at opposite edges; center slot `max-w-[14rem] min-w-0` + `text-overflow: ellipsis`) — it spends width, never a new height row. Any new play-screen chrome (banners, pills, readouts) must go beside/inside existing rows or use overlay/absolute positioning, never a plain new block under/around the board.
- **Container queries = web-only.** Cross-platform layout: flex + max-width. No `@container` in pure RN views.
- **Viewport shells:** root `h-dvh overflow-hidden` → `Shell` fills height (`flex flex-col min-h-0`). Scroll inside a child (`flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto cp-shell-scroll`), not body alone — lobby keeps Play (+ Last haul) as a shrink-0 footer outside that scroller; `.cp-lobby-play` owns bottom safe-area + shadow room (`padding-bottom: max(1.25rem, calc(1rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)))`). Lobby Shell: no `overflow-hidden`/`pb-0` on the column (clips the bar). Web: `.cp-shell-scroll` in `packages/ui` `theme.css` = `scrollbar-gutter: stable` + thin thumb — **no extra `padding-inline-end` on the outer scroll wrapper** (that shrinks nested Shell vs sticky Play Shell and clips How hard?/board rows on the right). Shell `px-4` clears the gutter.
- **Tailwind content-scan gotcha:** a custom `@layer components` rule is silently dropped from the build if its exact class string never appears literally in a scanned source file — `` `cp-word-chip-${variant}` `` never spells out `cp-word-chip-found`, so Tailwind purges it (no build error, no lint error, just a missing rule). Always write conditional custom classes as full literal strings in a ternary (`variant === "found" ? "cp-word-chip-found" : "cp-word-chip-missed"`), never string-interpolate the suffix. Verify with a computed-style check (chrome-devtools/Playwright `getComputedStyle`) when a bespoke class seems to have no effect — don't assume it's a specificity issue first.
- UI changes require interactive verify (pointer swipe for play) — see `.cursor/skills/verify-ui`. Layout bugs (clipping, overflow, sticky footers, `dvh`/safe-area): prefer **chrome-devtools MCP** (computed styles, box model, `scrollWidth`/overflow checks, screenshots at multiple widths) to find the actual root cause; Playwright stays fine for interaction smoke.
